---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Soha Sami">
  <section class="inner-hero shell" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow">About Soha</p>
    <h1>Economics.<br />Mathematics.<br /><em>Energy.</em></h1>
  </section>

  <section class="about-intro shell" data-reveal>
    <div class="about-intro-label">
      <span>01</span>
      <p>Background</p>
    </div>

    <div class="about-intro-copy">
      <p class="about-lead">
        I’m Soha, a student working across energy markets, quantitative finance and climate risk.
      </p>

      <p>
        I’m currently studying through the Erasmus Mundus GrEnFin programme in
        Greening Energy Market and Finance, alongside an MSc in Financial and
        Insurance Mathematics at LMU Munich.
      </p>

      <p>
        My academic path has taken me from New Delhi to Bologna, Paris and
        Munich. Each place has given me something different, from energy markets
        and finance to climate, quantitative modelling and risk.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="education-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <span class="section-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Education</p>
          <h2>Three degrees.<br /><em>One direction.</em></h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="education-list">
        <article class="education-item" data-reveal>
          <div class="education-year">2025–2027</div>
          <div class="education-content">
            <p class="education-type">CURRENT · ERASMUS MUNDUS</p>
            <h3>Erasmus Mundus GrEnFin</h3>
            <h4>Greening Energy Market and Finance</h4>
            <p>
              My main focus is the economics and finance of changing energy
              systems, with studies covering electricity markets, energy
              finance, climate and business, market design and quantitative
              approaches to energy.
            </p>
            <div class="education-universities">
              <span>Università di Bologna</span>
              <span>Université Paris Dauphine-PSL</span>
              <span>LMU Munich</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="education-item" data-reveal>
          <div class="education-year">2025–2027</div>
          <div class="education-content">
            <p class="education-type">GRADUATE STUDIES · MUNICH</p>
            <h3>MSc Financial and Insurance Mathematics</h3>
            <h4>Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München</h4>
            <p>
              At LMU, I am building the more technical side of my training,
              including stochastic modelling, quantitative risk management,
              financial mathematics, numerical methods and statistical modelling.
            </p>
            <div class="education-tags">
              <span>Stochastic Modelling</span>
              <span>Quantitative Risk</span>
              <span>Financial Mathematics</span>
              <span>Numerical Methods</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="education-item" data-reveal>
          <div class="education-year">2021–2025</div>
          <div class="education-content">
            <p class="education-type">UNDERGRADUATE · NEW DELHI</p>
            <h3>BA Economics & Mathematics</h3>
            <h4>University of Delhi</h4>
            <p>
              This is where I built the foundation for the work I do now,
              combining economics with mathematics, statistics and quantitative
              analysis.
            </p>
            <div class="education-tags">
              <span>Economics</span>
              <span>Mathematics</span>
              <span>Statistics</span>
              <span>Quantitative Analysis</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="journey-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <span class="section-number">03</span>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Academic journey</p>
          <h2>New Delhi →<br />Bologna → Paris → <em>Munich</em></h2>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="journey-grid">
        <div class="journey-place" data-reveal>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>New Delhi</h3>
          <p>Economics & Mathematics</p>
          <small>University of Delhi</small>
        </div>

        <div class="journey-place" data-reveal>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Bologna</h3>
          <p>Energy markets & finance</p>
          <small>Università di Bologna</small>
        </div>

        <div class="journey-place" data-reveal>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Paris</h3>
          <p>Climate & Business</p>
          <small>Paris Dauphine-PSL</small>
        </div>

        <div class="journey-place active" data-reveal>
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Munich</h3>
          <p>Financial & Insurance Mathematics</p>
          <small>LMU Munich</small>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="journey-copy" data-reveal>
        <p>
          Living and studying in Italy, France and Germany has also made me
          interested in the differences between the countries themselves. The
          academic cultures are different, and so are the industries and
          institutions shaping energy and finance. Moving between them has made
          European energy markets feel much less abstract to me.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-focus-section">
    <div class="shell about-focus-grid">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">What I am learning</p>
        <h2>What I am<br /><em>working on.</em></h2>
      </div>

      <div class="focus-columns" data-reveal>
        <div>
          <span>ENERGY</span>
          <p>Electricity markets</p>
          <p>Market design</p>
          <p>Renewable generation</p>
          <p>Flexibility</p>
          <p>Power price dynamics</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>QUANTITATIVE</span>
          <p>Stochastic modelling</p>
          <p>Quantitative risk management</p>
          <p>Numerical methods</p>
          <p>Monte Carlo simulation</p>
          <p>Dependence modelling</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <span>COMPUTATIONAL</span>
          <p>Python</p>
          <p>Statistical analysis</p>
          <p>Data pipelines</p>
          <p>Git & GitHub</p>
          <p>Reproducible research</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="scholarship-section">
    <div class="shell scholarship-grid" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Erasmus Mundus</p>
        <h2>Studying across<br /><em>Europe.</em></h2>
      </div>

      <div>
        <p class="scholarship-title">
          Erasmus Mundus Joint Master in Greening Energy Market and Finance
        </p>
        <p>
          The Erasmus Mundus scholarship is what made this international
          academic path possible. It has given me the chance to study energy
          markets and finance in different European settings and experience
          different approaches to the energy transition.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-end shell" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow">Currently</p>
    <h2>Energy markets, quantitative finance,<br /><em>and climate risk.</em></h2>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
